        <mxCell id="ovW" value="wave.ttl  coordination — passes, tickets, findings, confirmations, rulings" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="520" y="380" width="400" height="180" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ovL" value="lexicon.ttl  the symptom vocabulary — names for how work goes wrong" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="960" y="380" width="400" height="180" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ovp" value="" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1400" y="380" width="1100" height="560" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ovpt" value="The one sentence each cluster is defending" style="text;html=1;fontSize=15;align=left;fontColor=#333333;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1420" y="396" width="1060" height="26" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ovpb" value="A · IDENTITY — you present who you are; you never claim it. The substrate derives it from the verified connection.  B · STRUCTURE — a kernel declares its shape; the ground refuses what violates it. The 0/1/2 dependency count IS the Separation Axiom.  C · THE SEALED FACT — a fact carries who made it, under whose meaning, at which surface version, judged by which shape. All four are derived. Nothing is mutated; corrections append.  D · SURFACE — what you may do is DERIVED from what was materialized, not registered by hand. An affordance nobody derived is an affordance nobody can attribute.  E · GOVERNANCE — a change to meaning is proposed, voted and applied, and the apply must seal a Materialization in the same transaction. A bumped epoch with no Materialization cannot commit.  F · ADOPTION — proximity is not adoption. A file on disk is not in the enforcement surface; only a sealed Adoption naming its digest puts it there.  Read the tabs in order. A and B are what you ARE; C is what you SAY; D and E are what you may DO and how that changes; F is how you take on someone else&#39;s meaning." style="text;html=1;fontSize=12;align=left;fontColor=#333333;fontStyle=0;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1420" y="432" width="1060" height="490" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
