            <mxPoint as="offset" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="eb7" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=open;strokeColor=#82b366;strokeWidth=2;dashed=1;fontSize=19;" parent="1" source="DATA" target="TOOL" edge="1">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="eb7L" value="dependsOn" style="edgeLabel;html=1;fontSize=19;fontColor=#82b366;labelBackgroundColor=#FFFFFF;" parent="eb7" vertex="1" connectable="0">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
            <mxPoint as="offset" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="pb" value="" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1450" y="180" width="1050" height="880" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="pbt" value="How it works" style="text;html=1;fontSize=15;align=left;fontColor=#6c8ebf;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1470" y="196" width="1010" height="26" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="pbb" value="THE COUNT IS THE AXIOM. CK depends on nothing, TOOL on CK, DATA on CK and TOOL. Those counts are gated by sh:hasValue in the shape, so the Separation Axiom is ENFORCED rather than described. DATA cannot write CK; TOOL cannot rewrite shape.  WHAT EACH ORGAN IS FOR. CK — what you MEAN (0 deps, governed-only writes). TOOL — what you can DO (1 dep, read-only on the ontology). DATA — what you have DONE (2 deps, read-write). Meaning cannot be edited by the thing that merely acts.  ownedBy IS STAMPED. A client may declare its own STRUCTURE — Kernel plus three organs — and may NOT declare who owns it. Germination stamps ownedBy from the verified connection exactly as createdBy is derived. That single line is the difference between a kernel and a forgery.  MEASURED — WHY THIS WAS UNBUILDABLE. Until 0.4.43 no kernel could be germinated through the door at all, for three stacked reasons: ckp.validate aimed its scratch graph at the same id band pgrdf allocates data graphs from (59 live graphs at ordinary container pids; the core ontology at 1000000221); _body_to_ttl dropped ARRAYS in the overload seal actually calls, so hasOrgan minCount 3 could never be satisfied and ckp:Kernel was literally unsealable; and the sealed body named organs at …/kernel/organ/* while the graph declared them at …/organ/*, which the shape could not catch because it only counts and type-checks.  A NAME IS A TRANSPORT SEGMENT. A project name is one lowercase segment; NATS subjects are case-sensitive, so an uppercase or dotted name is a kernel nobody can address. germinate refuses it and names the slug to use." style="text;html=1;fontSize=20;align=left;fontColor=#333333;fontStyle=0;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1470" y="232" width="1010" height="810" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="c" name="C · The sealed fact">
    <mxGraphModel dx="5086" dy="1247" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="2600" pageHeight="1500" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="T" value="C · THE SEALED FACT" style="text;html=1;fontSize=30;align=left;fontColor=#000000;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="30" width="2000" height="34" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="S" value="Provenance is a consequence of sealing, never a claim inside it" style="text;html=1;fontSize=19;align=left;fontColor=#d79b00;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="70" width="2200" height="24" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="Instance" value="Instance — THE FOUR STAMPS  createdBy → Participant           who producedBy → Kernel                whose meaning sealedAtEpoch → integer            which surface conformsToShape → sh:NodeShape     judged by what" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;fontSize=19;align=left;spacingLeft=16;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="100" y="180" width="830" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="fence" value="preEnforcementEpoch → integer  A CLAIM, not a derivation. &quot;This row predates enforcement.&quot;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d79b00;fontSize=19;align=left;spacingLeft=16;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="610" y="390" width="620" height="80" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="Ledger" value="LedgerEntry  about · bodySha · sig prev → integer · ts" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;fontSize=19;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="640" y="600" width="290" height="140" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="Proof" value="Proof  about · method digest · verifiedAt" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;fontSize=19;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="950" y="600" width="290" height="140" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="Supersession" value="Supersession  supersedes → Instance" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;fontSize=19;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="610" width="290" height="110" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="Run" value="Run  runOf → Affordance realizes → TOOL startedAt · endedAt" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;fontSize=19;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="270" y="950" width="290" height="110" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ec1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=open;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=19;" parent="1" source="Instance" target="Ledger" edge="1">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ec1L" value="every seal APPENDS" style="edgeLabel;html=1;fontSize=19;fontColor=#b85450;labelBackgroundColor=#FFFFFF;" parent="ec1" vertex="1" connectable="0">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
            <mxPoint as="offset" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ec2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=open;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=19;" parent="1" source="Supersession" target="Instance" edge="1">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ec2L" value="supersedes" style="edgeLabel;html=1;fontSize=19;fontColor=#b85450;labelBackgroundColor=#FFFFFF;" parent="ec2" vertex="1" connectable="0">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
            <mxPoint as="offset" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ec3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=open;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=19;" parent="1" source="Instance" target="Run" edge="1">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ec3L" value="wasGeneratedBy" style="edgeLabel;html=1;fontSize=19;fontColor=#999999;labelBackgroundColor=#FFFFFF;" parent="ec3" vertex="1" connectable="0">
          <mxGeometry x="0.3" relative="1" as="geometry">
            <mxPoint as="offset" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="pc" value="" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d79b00;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1450" y="180" width="1050" height="830" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="pct" value="How it works" style="text;html=1;fontSize=15;align=left;fontColor=#d79b00;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1470" y="196" width="1010" height="26" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="pcb" value="FOUR DERIVED, ONE ASSERTED — and they look alike, which is the trap. createdBy, producedBy, sealedAtEpoch and conformsToShape are computed by the substrate; a body carrying them has them STRIPPED before the gate. preEnforcementEpoch is the opposite: a claim the caller makes, which a second party can check against the epoch it names. Grouping them is what nearly made the fence unusable — it was put on a &quot;never assert&quot; list, which would have refused the only honest way to mark a legacy row.  APPEND-ONLY IS WHAT MAKES CORRECTION POSSIBLE. seal hashes the body; verify compares the stored body to the LATEST ledger entry. So a correction cannot be an UPDATE — that would change the digest and make every corrected row read as tampered. It is a re-seal, which APPENDS. Proven from a second kernel: ledger seq 108 (original) and seq 110 (fenced) both survive, verify true.  conformsToShape IS THE SAFETY PROPERTY. It is present only when a shape actually TARGETS the type. Its absence is the substrate reporting that the SHACL gate selected no focus node and passed vacuously. Measured: an instance with an undeclared property AND a declared one carrying the wrong datatype sealed ok:true, verified:true, with a proof digest and a ledger entry — three stamps, no conformsToShape. A permanent, verified row that nothing judged.  verified ≠ judged. verified:true is the HMAC chain — the bytes are intact. conformsToShape is judgement — a shape looked at it. Rendering them side by side as equals is what makes &quot;sealed&quot; look like &quot;gated&quot;, and it is how a vacuous row gets past a careful reader." style="text;html=1;fontSize=19;align=left;fontColor=#333333;fontStyle=0;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1470" y="232" width="1010" height="760" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="d" name="D · Surface &amp; execution">
    <mxGraphModel dx="5086" dy="1247" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="2600" pageHeight="1500" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="T" value="D · SURFACE &amp;amp; EXECUTION" style="text;html=1;fontSize=30;align=left;fontColor=#000000;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="30" width="2000" height="34" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="S" value="What a kernel may do is DERIVED from what was materialized — never registered by hand" style="text;html=1;fontSize=18;align=left;fontColor=#82b366;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="80" y="70" width="2200" height="24" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="Materialization" value="Materialization  producesAffordance → Affordance producesEpoch → Epoch toEpoch → integer" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=19;fontStyle=1;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="100" y="180" width="360" height="150" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="Epoch" value="Epoch  surfaceDigest" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=19;fontStyle=1;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="740" y="180" width="280" height="110" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="Affordance" value="Affordance  inTopic · outTopic · plane inShape → sh:NodeShape delegate → boolean derivedBy → Materialization retiredAtEpoch → integer" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontSize=19;fontStyle=1;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="110" y="460" width="360" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="AffordanceUse" value="AffordanceUse  uses → Affordance consumer → Kernel provider → Kernel pinnedEpoch → integer" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;fontSize=19;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="750" y="430" width="290" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="RunD" value="Run  runOf → Affordance realizes → TOOL" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;fontSize=19;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="120" y="800" width="360" height="110" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="FailedMat" value="FailedMaterialization  the surface that did NOT compile" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;fontSize=19;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="610" y="800" width="290" height="110" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ed1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=open;strokeColor=#d6b656;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=19;" parent="1" source="Materialization" target="Affordance" edge="1">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ed1L" value="producesAffordance" style="edgeLabel;html=1;fontSize=19;fontColor=#d6b656;labelBackgroundColor=#FFFFFF;" parent="ed1" vertex="1" connectable="0">
          <mxGeometry x="-0.3" relative="1" as="geometry">
            <mxPoint as="offset" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ed2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=open;strokeColor=#d6b656;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=19;" parent="1" source="Materialization" target="Epoch" edge="1">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ed2L" value="producesEpoch" style="edgeLabel;html=1;fontSize=19;fontColor=#d6b656;labelBackgroundColor=#FFFFFF;" parent="ed2" vertex="1" connectable="0">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
            <mxPoint as="offset" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ed3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=open;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=19;" parent="1" source="AffordanceUse" target="Affordance" edge="1">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ed3L" value="uses" style="edgeLabel;html=1;fontSize=19;fontColor=#999999;labelBackgroundColor=#FFFFFF;" parent="ed3" vertex="1" connectable="0">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
            <mxPoint as="offset" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ed4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=open;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=19;" parent="1" source="RunD" target="Affordance" edge="1">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ed4L" value="runOf" style="edgeLabel;html=1;fontSize=19;fontColor=#999999;labelBackgroundColor=#FFFFFF;" parent="ed4" vertex="1" connectable="0">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
            <mxPoint as="offset" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="pd" value="" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#82b366;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1450" y="180" width="1050" height="880" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="pdt" value="How it works" style="text;html=1;fontSize=15;align=left;fontColor=#82b366;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1470" y="196" width="1010" height="26" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="pdb" value="AN AFFORDANCE IS DERIVED, NOT DECLARED. Materialization → producesAffordance is the only lawful origin. A hand-sealed Affordance comes back with no producedBy, no sealedAtEpoch and no conformsToShape — the substrate declining to attribute what it did not derive. Two such probes are on the bench right now; they are mine, and they should be superseded by a real materialization rather than retired.  THE PLANE DECIDES THE PATH. instance — ordinary verbs. query — SPARQL sealed as a plan, compiled into ckp.plans keyed (kernel, verb, epoch). derived — a computed value. governance — propose/vote/apply, which never execute as ordinary verbs.  RESOLUTION IS TWO-LAYERED, and both halves are load-bearing. A verb resolves against the CALLER&#39;s own registered surface first, then falls back to the surface seeded at install — which belongs to no kernel, because install runs before any kernel exists. Resolving only the caller made the seeded verbs unreachable for everyone; resolving only a fixed name made every kernel share one surface. That fixed name is exactly the defect that hid all day: dispatch asked registry_lookup(&#39;pgck&#39;, verb) for EVERY caller, so a verb a kernel registered, voted through and applied was invisible to its own owner.  outTopic DECLARES WHERE THE ANSWER GOES. It was NULL on every row, so a subscriber had to read the relay&#39;s Rust to learn the reply subject. It now states what the transport already implements: result.kernel...  AffordanceUse IS THE UNUSED HALF. pinnedEpoch plus consumer/provider is how a consumer records WHICH surface it was promised, so &quot;the provider moved on, what did I rely on?&quot; is answerable. The fleet has this and does not use it." style="text;html=1;fontSize=19;align=left;fontColor=#333333;fontStyle=0;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1470" y="232" width="1010" height="810" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="e" name="E · Governed plane">
    <mxGraphModel dx="3912" dy="959" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="2600" pageHeight="1500" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="T" value="E · GOVERNED PLANE" style="text;html=1;fontSize=22;align=left;fontColor=#000000;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="30" width="2000" height="34" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="S" value="A change to meaning is proposed, voted and applied — and the apply must seal a Materialization" style="text;html=1;fontSize=13;align=left;fontColor=#9673a6;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="70" width="2200" height="24" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="Proposal" value="Proposal  about · proposalOp proposalState requiresQuorum" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="100" y="380" width="320" height="160" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="Vote" value="Vote  about → Proposal voteValue (approve | reject)" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="290" y="120" width="320" height="160" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="Apply" value="ckp.apply  bumps the epoch AND seals a Materialization — same transaction" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1020" y="190" width="340" height="160" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="Ops" value="THE FOUR OPS WITH A PROJECTOR  add_class · add_property set_transition_map · add_affordance  An op with no projector is refused AT PROPOSE — never sealed as an inert &quot;applied&quot;." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontSize=12;align=left;spacingLeft=16;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="100" y="590" width="560" height="200" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="TransitionE" value="Transition  fromState · toState" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;fontSize=12;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="750" y="590" width="290" height="120" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ee1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=open;strokeColor=#9673a6;strokeWidth=2;" parent="1" source="Vote" target="Proposal" edge="1">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ee1L" value="about" style="edgeLabel;html=1;fontSize=11;fontColor=#9673a6;labelBackgroundColor=#FFFFFF;" parent="ee1" vertex="1" connectable="0">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
            <mxPoint as="offset" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ee2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=open;strokeColor=#9673a6;strokeWidth=2;" parent="1" source="Proposal" target="Apply" edge="1">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ee2L" value="at quorum" style="edgeLabel;html=1;fontSize=11;fontColor=#9673a6;labelBackgroundColor=#FFFFFF;" parent="ee2" vertex="1" connectable="0">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
            <mxPoint as="offset" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="pe" value="" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1450" y="190" width="1050" height="860" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="pet" value="How it works" style="text;html=1;fontSize=15;align=left;fontColor=#9673a6;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1470" y="206" width="1010" height="26" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="peb" value="THE EPOCH IS NOT A COUNTER. Apply bumps it, recompiles the plan surface, and seals a first-class Materialization that produces an Epoch carrying the surface digest — all in ONE transaction. If the Materialization or the Epoch fails its shape gate, the whole apply rolls back. A bumped epoch with no valid Materialization cannot commit, which is what makes &quot;show me the Materialization that produced this epoch, and re-derive the surface at that epoch&quot; answerable from the seals.  NO GOVERNED OP WITHOUT A PROJECTOR. An op that cannot project a change is refused at propose. Widening that set requires implementing a projector, not editing a list.  MEASURED — THE INERT EPOCH. The guard checked that the OP had a projector but never that the DETAIL carried anything to project. So an add_affordance with an empty detail sealed &quot;applied&quot;, bumped the epoch, registered nothing, and returned ok:true with graph_changed:false and no error on any surface. One epoch on this bench IS that inert applied — an epoch that logged nothing while reporting success. It is now refused at propose.  add_class ACCEPTED PROPERTIES AND DROPPED THEM, emitting one quad and reporting success. Because _type_admitted accepts a bare owl:Class, the result was not an unusable type — it was a type that admits instances NOTHING JUDGES. A vacuity generator, governed into existence through the sanctioned door.  ⚠ QUORUM 1 IS REHEARSAL. One proposer, one voter, one applier declares SHAPE, not consensus. Both integrity checks now running on this bench were sealed that way, and so was every governed change made today. Say so when you use it." style="text;html=1;fontSize=12;align=left;fontColor=#333333;fontStyle=0;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1470" y="242" width="1010" height="790" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="f" name="F · Adoption">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1800" dy="1200" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="2600" pageHeight="1500" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="T" value="F · ADOPTION" style="text;html=1;fontSize=22;align=left;fontColor=#000000;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="30" width="2000" height="34" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="S" value="Proximity is not adoption — a module joins the enforcement surface only by sealed digest" style="text;html=1;fontSize=13;align=left;fontColor=#d6b656;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="70" width="2200" height="24" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="Adoption" value="Adoption  adopts → Module sourceDigest  ^[0-9a-f]{64}$ intoProject → Project fromProject → Project intoEpoch · sourceEpoch" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="100" y="190" width="400" height="200" as="geometry" />
