        <mxCell id="ew4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=open;strokeColor=#82b366;strokeWidth=2;" edge="1" parent="1" source="wPass" target="wWave">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ew4L" value="ofWave" style="edgeLabel;html=1;fontSize=11;fontColor=#82b366;labelBackgroundColor=#FFFFFF;" vertex="1" connectable="0" parent="ew4">
          <mxGeometry x="0" relative="1" as="geometry">
            <mxPoint as="offset" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="pw" value="" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#82b366;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1450" y="190" width="1050" height="900" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="pwt" value="How it works" style="text;html=1;fontSize=15;align=left;fontColor=#82b366;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1470" y="206" width="1010" height="26" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="pwb" value="A TICKET IS ASSIGNED WORK — &quot;one unit of assigned work, owned by exactly one component for exactly one pass. Closes on confirmation, never on completion.&quot;  A FINDING IS NOT WORK — &quot;something measured that is not work. Unowned and unscheduled by default. It becomes a ticket only by explicit promotion.&quot; And since a component holds ONE ticket, promoting DISPLACES whatever it was doing.  THAT DISTINCTION DECIDES WHAT A NOTIFICATION IS. A notify that created a Ticket would conscript the recipient and silently evict their current work. A notify that creates a FINDING says: I measured something, it is not yours to do, and it becomes work only if you promote it. Promotion is the recipient&#39;s act.  CONFIRMATION IS NOT A VOTE. &quot;A second component measuring a ticket it does not own — the only thing that closes a ticket, and the reason self-report cannot.&quot; And evidence is &quot;the exact command anyone can re-run, and its output. A confirmation that cannot be re-run is an opinion.&quot; That is recheck, not quorum: it does not matter who says it, it matters that anyone can run it again.  THE CLOSED SETS ARE THE VALUE. defectKind — hole · gap · collision · omission · stale-overwrite · vacuity · misattribution. opKind — fourteen acts, and &quot;an act outside it is an act the process has not yet learned to see&quot;. findingState — closed-by-ruling is &quot;the cheapest close available: out of scope, permanently, for one sentence&quot;.  NOT IN v3.11 AT ALL: Notify · Message · Signal · Ask · Goal · Task. The shipped notify verb seals urn:ckp:board/Message, which NO shape targets — so it seals vacuously, with a caller-supplied &#39;from&#39;." style="text;html=1;fontSize=12;align=left;fontColor=#333333;fontStyle=0;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1470" y="242" width="1010" height="830" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="l" name="lexicon.ttl — symptoms">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1800" dy="1200" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="2600" pageHeight="1500" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="T" value="MODULE · lexicon.ttl" style="text;html=1;fontSize=22;align=left;fontColor=#000000;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="30" width="2000" height="34" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="S" value="urn:ckp:module/lexicon/v3.11 — adopted by digest ce9f20f4… — names for how work goes wrong" style="text;html=1;fontSize=13;align=left;fontColor=#b85450;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="70" width="2200" height="24" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="lS" value="Symptom" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="100" y="190" width="250" height="70" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="lP" value="Pattern" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="390" y="190" width="250" height="70" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="lR" value="Rule" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="680" y="190" width="250" height="70" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="lO" value="Outcome" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="970" y="190" width="250" height="70" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="lKinds" value="THE SYMPTOM CLASSES  VacuousGate — present, well-formed, never evaluated FalseGate — refuses the wrong thing UnreadGate — a rule nobody consulted Misattribution — named for where it was found,             not where it must be fixed StaleCitation — a rationale outliving its reason UncountedClaim · UnmeasuredConsequence BrokenSequence · HeldAct · RefutedAct · BenchOnly" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#b85450;fontSize=12;align=left;spacingLeft=16;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="100" y="320" width="560" height="290" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="lE" value="THE EDGES  causedBy — this symptom produced that one blocks / blockedBy — what cannot proceed symptom — the observable of a pattern recurrenceOf — THIS ONE AGAIN fromPattern · outcome · passDirector defectIn · defectOwner confirmedBy · confirmedTicketOwner  ruleState · enforcedBy · proposedAtPass refutedAtPass · instancesAtProposal" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#b85450;fontSize=12;align=left;spacingLeft=16;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="760" y="320" width="560" height="290" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="lToday" value="TODAY, IN ITS OWN VOCABULARY  VacuousGate      a row sealed verified, judged by nothing StaleCitation    &quot;SPARQL cannot express it&quot; — true until it was not Misattribution   createdBy:anon beside a verified ownedBy collision        two hardcoded names agreeing by accident stale-overwrite  a cached term id outliving its rolled-back row recurrenceOf     four overload-parity defects, one pattern, nothing counting" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#b85450;fontSize=12;align=left;spacingLeft=16;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="100" y="660" width="1220" height="220" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="pl" value="" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#b85450;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1450" y="190" width="1050" height="880" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="plt" value="How it works" style="text;html=1;fontSize=15;align=left;fontColor=#b85450;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1470" y="206" width="1010" height="26" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="plb" value="THIS MODULE NAMES FAILURE MODES, NOT FAILURES. A Symptom is what you observe; a Pattern is the shape behind it; a Rule is what the wave decided to do about it; an Outcome is what happened. Together they turn &quot;this keeps going wrong&quot; from an impression into a query.  recurrenceOf IS THE ONE THAT PAYS FOR ITSELF. Any single defect looks like bad luck. The fourth instance of the same pattern is a design problem — but only if something counted. Four overload-parity defects landed in one day here, each a CREATE OR REPLACE matching the wrong signature, and nothing in the record connected them.  THE NAMES ARE NOT GENERIC, WHICH IS WHY THEY ARE USEFUL. VacuousGate is not &quot;a bug&quot; — it is precisely a gate that ran, passed, and selected nothing. Once you have the word, the fix is obvious: assert that the check SELECTED something, not merely that it did not fail. Three separate defects here had exactly that signature.  StaleCitation IS THE ONE TO WATCH IN A FLEET. A rationale recorded when a limitation was real, cited long after the limitation was lifted. A neighbouring kernel raised exactly this against a claim made here — &quot;the moment the engine ships negation, the rationale becomes a StaleCitation nobody revisits&quot; — and it was right.  HOW IT PAIRS WITH wave. A Finding carries what was measured; lexicon:symptom says WHAT KIND of wrong it is; lexicon:defectIn says where; lexicon:blocks says what it stops. That is a notification with a diagnosis attached, and none of it needs a new ontology." style="text;html=1;fontSize=12;align=left;fontColor=#333333;fontStyle=0;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1470" y="242" width="1010" height="810" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
